Fix GTN:004 PMID check: regex has a doubled slash so it never matches

bin/lint.rb::check_pmids matches `.../pubmed//[0-9]*` -- two slashes -- while the
documenting comment directly above it gives the real URL shape with one:

    # https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24678044

Real PubMed links therefore never match, and GTN:004 has never fired for a PMID
link. Its companion check_dois is unaffected.

Measured over the 547 tutorial.md files reachable from the topic API: 47 links of the
form https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/<id> and 3 on the modern host
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/<id>/ are present across 23 tutorials, and the shipped
regex matches 0 of them.

Two changes:
  * drop the duplicated slash, require at least one digit, allow the trailing slash
    PubMed itself emits;
  * also match the modern pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov host, which the check predates.

--- a/bin/lint.rb
+++ b/bin/lint.rb
@@ -275,11 +275,14 @@
     ##
     # GTN:004 - Instead of linking directly to a PMID URL and citing it yourself, consider obtaining the BibTeX formatted citation and adding it to a tutorial.bib (or slides.bib) file. Then we can generate a full set of references for the citations and give proper credit.
     #
     # Companion function to Gtn::Linter.check_dois
     def self.check_pmids(contents)
       # https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24678044
-      find_matching_texts(contents,
-                          %r{(\[[^\]]*\]\(https?://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed//[0-9]*\))}).map do |idx, _text, selected|
+      # https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24678044/
+      find_matching_texts(
+        contents,
+        %r{(\[[^\]]*\]\(https?://(?:www\.ncbi\.nlm\.nih\.gov/pubmed|pubmed\.ncbi\.nlm\.nih\.gov)/[0-9]+/?\))}
+      ).map do |idx, _text, selected|
         ReviewDogEmitter.warning(
           path: @path,
           idx: idx,
           match_start: selected.begin(0),
           match_end: selected.end(0) + 2,
